6. **The cells LIFT functions by the FIRST regex match, and `settings.js` declares `escapeHtml` TWICE (MEASURED).** `extractFunction` runs `new RegExp(\`(?:async\\s+)?function\\s+${name}\\s*\\(\`).exec(src)` (test :55-:64), so `lift(…, ['escapeHtml'])` on settings.js takes the declaration at **:89** (`if (typeof text !== 'string') return text;`). settings.js has a second at **:2436** (`if (typeof text !== 'string') return String(text || '');`). If both sit in the same function scope, the browser binds the LATER one (declaration hoisting), so the cell and the browser may run different helpers at :1701. For a string input both map the same five characters identically (READ ONLY), so the expected effect is nil; **which one binds is UNMEASURED** (needs a scope parse or the browser itself: b1's settings arm). index.js's lifted helper is :109 (`div.textContent = text; return div.innerHTML;`, escapes `&` `<` `>`, not quotes; every index.js site is a text context, READ ONLY). first-run-setup.js and chart-details.js each gain a NEW local five-character `escapeHtml` (:2933, :533).
7. **The offline chat's AI answer was HTML before and is TEXT now (MEASURED source; consequence READ-ONLY-INFERRED).** `addMessage(content)` (index-offline.js :77-:89 at `3047ae9`) is called with the user's query AND with `result.response` from `POST /api/chat` and with fixed AI-off sentences. Before: `innerHTML = \`<strong>…:</strong> ${content}\`` (the server answer parsed as markup). After: a `<strong>` node + a text node. The server builds `response` from `displayResponse` (server.js :7169-:7219); a grep for `<br>`/`<strong>`/`<b>` literals in `backend/` finds only an email body (server.js :21754), and the main page's `formatAIResponse` already escapes the AI text before formatting (index.js `const safeText = escapeHtml(text);`). **So the change is invisible for plain-text answers; an answer carrying a literal `&amp;`, `<b>` or `<br>` would now show those characters.** The builder's render-identity covers ONE ordinary message (242 chars). b2 must include answers with `&`, `<`, a newline and a markdown-ish line.
