## 2. Tier and severity rules
**TIER 1:** a gated tree differing from its proof in ANY path but the counts file is a **Blocker**; a payload that EXECUTES (marker set, element created, `GET /x` issued, dialog) on the branch at ANY of the 8 sites or the errorCode path, in the browser or in a cell, is a **Blocker**; an escape that is insufficient for the context it writes into (attribute vs text, `document.write` vs `innerHTML`) is a **Major** if a cell or browser arm shows markup surviving, else a **Minor** with READ ONLY; a revert of one fix that leaves every cell green (the cell does not guard its site, C-40) is a **Major**; a payload that does NOT execute on the BASE in the browser makes that b1 arm **VOID** (the control did not fire), never a pass; a visible difference between base and branch for an ORDINARY value (DOM text, element screenshot, layout box) is a **Major** (ANSWER-12: *"If a site needs any visible change, STOP and ask"*) unless it is the LoadingManager attribute named in the READY; an AI answer, button label or error panel that renders on base and not on branch is a **Major**; the cell and the browser binding DIFFERENT helpers (WRONG 6) with any observable difference is a **Minor**, with none an **N27**; a full verify red, a test name lost outside C-57/C-133, or a counts blob that disagrees with the verify is a **Major**; a NEW CodeQL alert on the PR head in changed code (high+ or rule severity `error`) is a **Blocker** for landing (C-190); a lockfile or package.json blob ≠ main's is a **Major**; deploy-demo NOT provably skipping is a **Blocker** for landing (Tuesday's call); a NEW gitleaks finding is a **Blocker**; a false READY claim is a **Minor**; the builder's flagged server/AI fields (WRONG 11) are **N27** (out of these alerts; candidate ticket), never a finding against RD-778; #28 (RD-790) is out of scope, named. **Severity is yours; priority is Tuesday's.** **Who is waiting:** merge author **NexusAI-O (S101O)**; **RD-771 is stacked on rd-778** (ANSWER-12: *"Stack it on rd-778 because the files are shared."*).

